How the automatic narrator works (and its limits)
Before speaking, the player divides your story into small beats, identifies dialogue and likely speakers, and detects action, humor, suspense, and soothing language. It then chooses a speech rate, pitch, volume, and pause length per beat. It gradually changes its delivery during the bedtime ending.
This is a **local, rule-based prototype**—not a connected AI model. It interprets cues automatically but may occasionally mistake a character or emotional tone. Voice quality and pitch support vary across iPhones and browsers. The reading uses your device's built-in speech synthesis, so audio stays on the device and no audio file is created. Safari may require the page to be opened as a website, rather than in a file preview.
For direct ChatGPT Voice storytelling, ask: “Be the Pantheon adaptive bedtime narrator: infer each character, emotion, joke, action, and transition without announcing labels. Perform dynamically, leave room for laughter, and gradually slow and soften the final quarter.” Voice mode's actual delivery controls depend on the selected voice system.
Single-file demo · Works without accounts, API keys, or subscriptions. Press Play once to allow speech on your device. Nothing you type is sent to a server by this page.
